    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0593" n="581" sameAs="frus:frus1945v02/pg581"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Council/11–2645: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-26">November 26,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received November 26—5:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2298. Personal for Secretary Byrnes. Situation serious. Unilateral action deeply
                    resented by both Bevin and Cabinet. Bevin refuses to talk tonight or to attend
                    conference Moscow. Information on suggested conference received last night by
                    Foreign Office from Clark Kerr<anchor n="29" xml:id="d205-f1"/> from Moscow
                    without simultaneous notice to British.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d205-f2"/>
                    <pb facs="0594" n="582" xml:id="pg582"/> Bevin realizes that his own party has
                    been seriously critical of his pro-United States position and effort to join
                    with you in forcing recognition of democratic procedures in Eastern European
                    countries. I have persuaded him to come to the Embassy tomorrow at 3:30 London
                    time to talk with you on teletype. I am meeting him tomorrow morning.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d205-f1" n="29" xml:id="d205-f1-content">
                <p>Sir Archibald Clark Kerr, British Ambassador to the Soviet Union.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d205-f2" n="30" xml:id="d205-f2-content">
                <p>This sentence apparently refers to the fact that the British learned of the
                    American proposal for a meeting of Foreign Ministers from their Embassy in
                    Moscow before the Secretary’s message to Bevin (telegram 10236, November 25, to
                    London, <ref target="#pg580">p. 580</ref>) was delivered to Bevin on the
                    afternoon of November 26.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
